# 28 - Incremental Load (Delta) Practical (Real DE Work)

This practical covers:
- What is incremental load
- Batch ID concept
- MERGE pattern for incremental loads
- Insert + update logic
- Idempotency concept (intro)
- Best practices

Incremental load is one of the most important real DE topics.

---

## 0) Setup

We will maintain a Silver table and apply new batch incrementally.

---

## 1) Create Initial Silver Table (Target)

```python
from pyspark.sql.functions import current_timestamp

target_data = [
    (1, "PRAMOD", "IT", 50000),
    (2, "AKASH", "HR", 60000),
    (3, "RAHUL", "IT", 45000),
]

target_df = spark.createDataFrame(target_data, ["id", "name", "dept", "salary"])

silver_path = "/tmp/delta/silver/employees_incremental"

target_df = target_df     .withColumn("created_at", current_timestamp())     .withColumn("updated_at", current_timestamp())

target_df.write.format("delta").mode("overwrite").save(silver_path)
```

---

## 2) New Batch Data (Source)

This batch contains:
- update id=2 salary
- insert id=4

```python
source_data = [
    (2, "AKASH", "HR", 65000),
    (4, "NEHA", "FINANCE", 70000)
]

source_df = spark.createDataFrame(source_data, ["id", "name", "dept", "salary"])
```

---

## 3) MERGE for Incremental Load

```python
source_df.createOrReplaceTempView("source_emp")

spark.sql(f"""
MERGE INTO delta.`{silver_path}` AS t
USING source_emp AS s
ON t.id = s.id
WHEN MATCHED THEN UPDATE SET
  t.name = s.name,
  t.dept = s.dept,
  t.salary = s.salary,
  t.updated_at = current_timestamp()
WHEN NOT MATCHED THEN INSERT (
  id, name, dept, salary, created_at, updated_at
) VALUES (
  s.id, s.name, s.dept, s.salary, current_timestamp(), current_timestamp()
)
""")
```

---

## 4) Validate Output

```python
spark.read.format("delta").load(silver_path).show(truncate=False)
```

Expected:
- id=2 salary updated
- id=4 inserted

---

## 5) Best Practices

✅ Always use MERGE for incremental updates  
✅ Maintain created_at and updated_at  
✅ Use a primary key for merge condition  
✅ Track batch_id in real pipelines  
✅ Use deduplication before merge  

---

## 6) Summary

- Incremental load updates existing rows and inserts new rows.
- MERGE is standard approach in Delta.
- Audit columns are important.

